# THE FRONTEND. `web/.dockerignore` does NOT cover this: it applies only to the frontend
# service, whose build context is ./web. The backend and migrate services build from `.`,
# which includes web/ in its entirety — so without these lines, 297MB of node_modules
# across ~50k small files is packed into the Python image's context and written into a
# layer. That is what turns "exporting to image" into a 20-minute step on Docker Desktop
# for Windows, where every one of those files crosses the WSL2 filesystem boundary.
#
# The Python image needs nothing from web/ at all: nginx serves the SPA from its own image.
web/

# The legacy Chroma directory. Chroma was removed in P2 (retrieval moved to Postgres +
# pgvector), so this is 39MB of dead weight that would otherwise ship in every image.
vector_store/

# Local eval/test artefacts — regenerated, never read by the running service.
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
scripts/

__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
env
venv
.venv
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt
.tox
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.log
.git
.gitignore
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.hypotheses
test_api.ipynb
LOG_FILE
